WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.780
"Do not go gentle into that good night"

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.400
"Old age should burn and rave at close of day"

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:11.849
"Rage, rage"

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:14.160
"Against the dying of the light"

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:19.469
The light meant everything to Gwyn, for before light he was nothing.

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:27.840
Imagine being a nameless member of some primitive congregation, barely scraping by in a harsh dark world.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:34.020
Then you come across a most glorious sight - light, and by that light

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:40.780
you find a soul. Not just any soul, but the most powerful soul. One that carries with it the power -

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:46.900
no, the responsibility - to lift your race out of the shadows onto, the surface where the dragons dwell.

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:53.129
Gwyn did not win this first war overnight. We forget this, but during the age of ancients,

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:55.880
there was still time for the Lords to rise.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.440
Civilizations were built,

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:01.680
alliances were forged, loyal Knights were appointed and

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:06.780
betrayers were born, for after disparity came creatures that were not born equal.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:12.820
Creatures like Seath who lived without the immortal stone scales of his brethren.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.960
With his mortality came a desperation,

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:23.140
an ambition, a jealousy; things the stone dragons never had and could never understand.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:29.520
And so, with their secrets betrayed by the pale drake, the dragons' homes were burned to ash,

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:34.049
their scales were pierced by lightning and their flesh was exposed to disease.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:40.439
The war was won and Gwyn could have eliminated Seath here, but he chose not to.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:47.880
Instead he did just the opposite. He granted Seath a piece of his very own soul. He elevated him to the peerage,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:54.960
he granted him dukedom and also the hand of his daughter, Gwynevere, with whom he could sire royal children.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:01.940
Honouring Seath like this ended up costing Gwyn his closest battle compatriot, Havel the Rock,

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:05.980
who harbored this deep hatred against the scaleless dragon.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:10.200
Havel is not found in game, but deep within an Anor Londo

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.320
behind an illusionary wall and

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:19.919
protected by a mimic, are his armaments, alongside the occult weaponry designed to kill a God.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:26.560
From this we can guess that Havel nursed this resentment for Gwyn, though it seems he never acted on it.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.800
At this time, after all, Gwyn was surrounded by his entourage of knights,

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:36.419
many of them wistfully craving this return to the combat that had once given them purpose.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:44.760
Gwyn would repeat this behavior throughout the Age of Fire, keeping his friends close and his enemies even closer,

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:49.799
for fire was at its peak, and the whole world was charmed by its brilliance.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:55.619
"Good men, the last wave by, crying how bright,"

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:00.840
"Their frail deeds might have danced in a green bay"

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.160
"Rage, rage"

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.220
"against the dying of the light"

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:13.679
To Nito, Gwyn permitted a quiet domain for all of the deceased, and in return Nito never did spread death to the gods.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:19.499
Over in Izalith, the Witch was tolerated despite spawning her creatures of chaos.

00:03:19.959 --> 00:03:25.139
But there was a fourth Lord - one that I didn't mention when talking about the dragon wars,

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:31.720
but one who took part in them just the same - the furtive pygmy race and their descendants.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.000
The Pygmy Lords, squirreling away a soul of dark,

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:39.360
represented the most significant threat to Gwyn's Age of Fire.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.340
So what do you think Gwyn did?

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:43.540
Exterminate them? No.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:51.140
Instead, Gwyn indebted them with the greatest gifts of all. While the Pygmy Lords waited patiently for light to fade,

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:53.459
Gwyn twisted their fate.

00:03:53.709 --> 00:03:59.459
Prop up this tiny race, bathe them in the glory of the light, blinds them with its brilliance,

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:02.850
give them a crown, a Ringed City, his youngest daughter.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:09.980
Let them indulge in bounty and, while they're still weak, raise a dragon to watch over them, seal their dark with fire and

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.150
shackle them to mortality.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:17.140
Let them spread across the earth and forget their heritage, their accomplishments.

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:22.120
Let the origins of humanity be buried, out of sight and out of mind.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.980
So, the pygmies were walled off,

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:31.820
safe, in a city that exists only at the end of the world. Most of them stayed there forever,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:40.520
happily subservient to their princess Filianore or who's very slumber was a miracle that was designed to prevent time from passing.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:47.030
Meanwhile humans, the pygmies' descendants, had spread to the outside world and out there,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:49.900
they too warmed themselves by fire.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:56.040
However, unbeknownst to most of them, this ran counter to their true nature.

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:01.480
In the dark there are no shadows, but where fire resides shadows twist and shrivel.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:07.970
So, some members of the dark did sense that something was wrong and they began to ram against their shackles.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:12.160
First, the Mad King was born to the pygmies and

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:18.700
he was undying, as the dark should be, so he was held in a dark room until the end of time.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:26.100
Later, yet another Pygmy Lord would go on to spawn an Abyss when he was unearthed in Oolacile.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:31.960
And, over time, even mankind turned into monsters. This hollowing process that

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:37.700
unfairly became attributed to their darkness instead of the fire the branded them.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.460
"Though wise men at their end know dark is right"

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:46.240
"because their words had forked no lightning"

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:50.040
"They do not go gentle into that good night"

00:05:51.349 --> 00:05:54.188
Gwyn's favored tool of control was the church.

00:05:54.889 --> 00:05:58.268
Something he had used to great effect already in the Ringed City,

00:05:58.269 --> 00:06:02.769
and he would use it again now to indoctrinate the people of the wider world.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:09.480
Gwyn the White was their deity of worship and Lloyd the Gray was at its head,

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:13.140
acting as a sort of intermediary between gods and humans.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:16.419
They framed undeath as a terrible sin,

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:22.238
and so the undead became the subjects of undead hunts led by cleric knights,

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:29.408
charged to cleanse the unholy. And if such a cleric, god forbid, actually became undead themselves,

00:06:29.629 --> 00:06:31.629
then there was a solution to that too.

00:06:31.909 --> 00:06:38.049
Such ironically cursed humans were shipped off to Lordran and given a new holy mission:

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:44.500
retrieve the right of kindling from the deadly catacombs, and if you should fail, well, so what?

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:48.920
Gwyn had basically dressed up exile for his undead clerics.

00:06:49.339 --> 00:06:55.719
But one man whose exile he did not spin, for once, was the banishment of his firstborn son.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:02.499
The Nameless King, God of War and leader of the Sunlight Covenant, had his godhood

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:06.980
rescinded after it was discovered that he was fraternizing with dragons.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:09.740
This was something he covered up.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:17.640
In addition, it seems like Gwyn's captain of the guard, Ornstein, went on to leave his post in favor of the Nameless King,

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:25.840
and so too - it appears - did Havel. whose knights arise in the Nameless King's defense at Arch Dragon Peak.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:29.240
A war had been fought in the name of disparity,

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:36.560
yet, how righteous, truly, was their war against the ancient, unchanging, everlasting dragons,

00:07:37.339 --> 00:07:41.259
when Gwyn himself refused to cede to the natural order?

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:48.320
But Gwynn's manipulation would not last for, the Nameless King was just a crack in the dam,

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.960
and the wall was set to burst.

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:58.359
"Wild men who caught and sang the Sun in flight, and learn, too late, they grieved it on its way"

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.929
"Do not go gentle into that good night"

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.670
Many alliances broke, seemingly all at once.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:13.840
Gravelord Nito had become increasingly reclusive and the Rite of Kindling had been lost within his domain,

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:19.760
Izalith had defiled flame and Gwyn's war against her demons had weakened his armies,

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:26.800
Seath was trending towards madness, the Way of White had begun to worship Lloyd instead and

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:34.280
there were even whispers that Kaath, one of the primordial serpents, had begun speaking the truth about the Pygmy Lords.

00:08:34.789 --> 00:08:36.789
Gwynn's light was waning.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:43.330
Illusions could keep it alive no longer and some people waited for a Dark Lord to be born amongst humans.

00:08:43.789 --> 00:08:47.139
Was Kaath right? Was he fighting against the inevitable?

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:52.059
Had he found the wrong soul? No, he was Lord Gwyn,

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.949
august magnificence, and if he was not yet worthy of worship,

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:02.020
then it was because he had not yet made a great enough sacrifice.

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:04.100
So Gwyn would link the fire,

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:08.080
leave a mark, perform the miracle that was so great,

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:15.720
a sacrifice so complete, that it would bring the world back from the brink of darkness, and it worked well. Too well.

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:21.680
Gywn was consumed and, with his dying breath, utterly defied disparity.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.320
The world became cursed.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:30.040
And from this point on every time an Age of Fire dwindled, the souls of Lords would flourish anew,

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.900
so that it could all play out again.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:40.220
The timeline of fire had warped. It had turned from a straight line, linked into a circle,

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:45.340
becoming this wall containing the rightful Age of Dark until the end of time.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:51.420
Eventually, as the world burned, out over and over again,

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:53.680
ash itself would arise.

00:09:53.800 --> 00:10:00.420
A new being, created from a thousand failures who had tried to link the fire over the years.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.240
But ash did not belong in this world, and honestly,

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:10.959
they had more in common with the beings of the Painted World, where all of fire's discarded things reside.

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.719
So, they fought for a new purpose:

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:22.680
to reunite the Dark Soul, and to paint a new world with it, so that they could escape the ashen wasteland that Gwyn had created.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:28.380
And so, far away, at the very end of the world, one of the first victims of the curse,

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:31.689
Slave Knight Gael, hollowed beyond belief,

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:38.409
also sacrificed himself for a new world, and he did not go gentle into that good night.

00:10:39.529 --> 00:10:43.569
"Grave men near death who see with blinding sight"

00:10:44.779 --> 00:10:48.069
"Blind eyes could blaze like meteors and be gay"

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.100
"Rage, rage"

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:54.300
"Against the dying of the light"

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:57.280
"And you,"

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.160
"my father,"

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:01.160
"there, on the sad height,"

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.020
"curse,"

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.800
"bless me now with your fierce tears, I pray"

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.699
"Do not go gentle into that good night."

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.220
"Rage"

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:13.880
"Rage"

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.380
"Against the dying of the light"

